    "title": "Artemis II is headed back to Earth. What time is the splashdown?",
    "text": "SPACEWhen does Artemis II crew return to Earth? See timeline, photosSamantha Neely Eric LagattaUSA TODAY NETWORK - FloridaApril 8, 2026Updated April 9, 2026, 11:45 a.m. ETSee updated coverage on when Artemis II returns to Earth this week here.After completing its mission of orbiting the moon, the Artemis II is now headed back home to Earth.Launching April 1 from Cape Canaveral, Florida, the 10-day mission primarily serves as a test flight, with the four-person crew testing systems and hardware ahead of a future moon landing. Under the Artemis campaign, NASA intends to eventually return astronauts to the surface of the moon for the first time since the Apollo missions ended in 1972.",
